    "['ptp clock', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset protocols ptp clock-mode boundary\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- Juniper uses `set protocols ptp` as the base for PTP configuration\\n- The `clock-mode boundary` corresponds to Cisco's `ptp clock` command when combined with `ptp device-type t-bc` (Telecom Boundary Clock)\\n- This establishes the router as a PTP boundary clock in the network hierarchy\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary'}]]": 1,
    "['ptp profile global [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ptp profile g.8275.1', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ptp profile g.8275.1', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the equivalent Juniper configuration command for the Cisco `ptp profile global g.8275.1`:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols ptp profile g.8275.1\\n##\\n\\nThis command configures the PTP (Precision Time Protocol) profile to use the G.8275.1 standard on a Juniper router, which is equivalent to the Cisco command specifying the global profile as G.8275.1.\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols ptp profile g.8275.1'}]]": 1,
    "['ptp device-type [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nset protocols ptp clock-mode boundary\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Cisco `ptp device-type t-bc` command configures the device as a Telecom Boundary Clock (T-BC) in PTP (Precision Time Protocol). The equivalent Juniper command is `set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary`, which also sets the device to operate as a boundary clock in PTP synchronization.', 'trans_template': 'set protocols ptp clock-mode boundary'}]]": 1,
