    "['no shutdown', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, in Junos operational mode (not configuration mode), the equivalent would be:\\n##\\nactivate interfaces ge-1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent depends on context. In configuration mode, `no shutdown` translates to `disable false` (since interfaces are disabled by default in Junos). In operational mode, it translates to `activate`. I've provided both common interpretations, with the configuration mode version being the more direct equivalent.\", 'trans_template': 'set interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false'}, {'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'activate interfaces ge-1/0/0', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"##\\nset interfaces ge-1/0/0 disable false\\n##\\n\\nAlternatively, in Junos operational mode (not configuration mode), the equivalent would be:\\n##\\nactivate interfaces ge-1/0/0\\n##\\n\\nNote: The Juniper equivalent depends on context. In configuration mode, `no shutdown` translates to `disable false` (since interfaces are disabled by default in Junos). In operational mode, it translates to `activate`. I've provided both common interpretations, with the configuration mode version being the more direct equivalent.\", 'trans_template': 'activate interfaces ge-1/0/0'}]]": 1,
